## Django Views Guidelines

### View Types

- Use Django's class-based views (CBVs) for complex API endpoints and CRUD operations
- Prefer function-based views (FBVs) for simple logic and WebSocket consumers
- Use DRF ViewSets for RESTful API endpoints
- Implement APIView for custom API behavior

### Error Handling

- Implement comprehensive error handling at the view level
- Use Django's built-in error handling mechanisms
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes for API responses
- Handle WebSocket connection errors gracefully
- Use try-except blocks for business logic exceptions

### Request Handling

- Keep business logic in models and forms; keep views focused on request handling
- Validate request data using DRF serializers
- Implement proper authentication and authorization
- Handle file uploads for media content
- Process WebSocket messages asynchronously

### Performance

- Use select_related and prefetch_related for database queries
- Implement caching for frequently accessed data
- Use background tasks (Celery) for heavy operations
- Optimize WebSocket message handling

### Security

- Validate all input data
- Implement proper permission checks
- Use CSRF protection for form submissions
- Sanitize user inputs
